{"id": "EUVD-2026-32773", "enisaUuid": "6074d471-0883-38bb-9bfe-494f460ff849", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nALSA: usb-audio: Avoid potential endless loop in convert_chmap_v3()\n\nThe convert_chmap_v3() has a loop with its increment size of\ncs_desc->wLength, but we forgot to validate cs_desc->wLength itself,\nwhich may lead to potential endless loop by a malformed descriptor.\n\nAdd a proper size check to abort the loop for plugging the hole.", "datePublished": "2026-05-28T09:36:02", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-15T01:20:47", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/076d5d13eb9c1ad259a7f246149f6676c62285f9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/316aa0b1e3c5600eae5ab876394c1ac70e6db581", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/24a40df79307ca7ca0eec0889361cf6ac146d72a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e0e3dcf48189603f3865f1a0b799b3b42baae96d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4e0ee232ebe3df04874125d7c7f3e6c25ea5483d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/be09b47ed8677d76962e3240c145502e2ad9f3c8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/fa5b19ce69067874b1413f3c2027563bae8c2cb3", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6e7247d8f5fefeceb0bb9cc80a5388a636b219cd"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-46146", "GHSA-pvph-jwxq-qcxw"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "11f396bd-6adb-338d-8639-84f5f64cb761", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.10.258"}, {"id": "17e9034a-e5bc-37f1-b05b-36cf48360667", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.12.43 <6.12.88"}, {"id": "1a1201bd-1929-33bc-be6f-b40abfb485f0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.4.297 <5.5"}, {"id": "1eb9e22b-de72-3ea8-a08f-4a5aa130373c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ecfd41166b72b67d3bdeb88d224ff445f6163869 <fa5b19ce69067874b1413f3c2027563bae8c2cb3"}, {"id": "2c016ec9-bf4